Audited against project-instructions.md **v1.2.8**. The prior audit named v1.2.4,
superseded in flight by four revisions of a new Temporary Files rule — the last
of which withdrew part of an earlier one. Governance required the compliance gate
to be re-run before this phase gate; it was re-run twice, at v1.2.7 (T074) and
again at v1.2.8 (recorded in plan.md:30-31) when E006's merge brought the
withdrawal. T076 corrected this line, which still named v1.2.7 after the second
re-run.

Three QC iterations found 28 defects. Each iteration found that the previous
one's fixes had left something overstated, and the pattern is worth naming: every
finding after iteration 1 was a claim that did not match what the repository
does, rather than a fault in what it does. All 28 are closed:

  Iteration 1 (T053-T065)
    T053  Principle VII — the security limitation record stated two falsehoods
          and its reversal trigger had fired.
    T054  FR-042 — the scoping control was absent in the empty-filter state.
    T055  FR-029 — the row-level stale mark was unimplemented.
    T056  FR-051 — bounded forms were not announced as words.
    T057  The E2E seed truncated the shared development database.
    T058-T065  Test-coverage, provenance and accuracy gaps.

  Iteration 2 (T066-T075) — six of ten were iteration 1's own claims
    T066  T055's fix added a per-row `as_of_is_stale` field and widened the
          contract to admit it. FR-029 says the mark "needs no new figure and no
          new field" and FR-027 closes the secondary region at three items. The
          field is gone; the interface composes the mark from
          `meta.forecast_run.stale`, and the contract is back to three.
    T067  T060's three properties read through a helper defined in the test file
          rather than through `rows.miss_probability`, and one of them asserted
          `x == x`. They now drive production code: mutating the survival read
          with a complement, or with an off-by-one, fails them.
    T068  tasks.md claimed a `test:` commit precedes each `feat:` commit. It
          does not, and the sentence is corrected rather than back-filled.
    T069  The invocation-record test issued no adjustment-carrying request,
          which is the half of FR-035 that was not blocked on E008.
    T070  plan.md recorded a Playwright request-recording observation that does
          not exist; the weaker source assertion that does is now what it says.
    T071  Three task entries named files that were never created.
    T072  plan.md recorded the benchmark population as "~200 open lines"; it is
          16. Corrected to what is measured.
    T073  The type-scale assertion measured the secondary container rather than
          its descendants, so the mark T055 added sat unchecked.
    T074  The compliance re-audit against v1.2.7.
    T075  `src/api` did not pin `--basetemp`, so its tests wrote to the shared
          system temp directory. Pinned, and measured by
          `tests/test_scratch_location.py` rather than declared.

  Iteration 3 (T076-T080) — all five were this file or the plan overstating
    T076  This marker named v1.2.7 after the re-audit at v1.2.8.
    T077  This marker's root-check figure read 249; measured 292. Its import
          contract count read 3 with no scope named; the repository keeps 11
          across three entries, of which src/api's 3 are E010's.
    T078  T071 corrected the three task entries it was filed for and left the
          same two names standing at five points in plan.md and once more in
          tasks.md's own Dependencies section.
    T079  T073 corrected the font-weight half of the type-scale assertion and
          left the font-size half beside it measuring the container. Now
          measured over descendants, and mutation-checked: a descendant set to
          2rem fails it at 32 px against a 16 px primary, while the container
          stays at 14 px — which is why the original passed.
    T080  This marker listed mypy among the checks E010 passes. No mypy runs
          over E010's code.

Reported, outside E010's scope:
  The root, `src/model` and `src/gateway` pytest configurations do not pin
  `--basetemp`. Same rule, other epics' entries.

  SC-017 and SC-018 are measured against the frozen fixture's 16 lines. The
  margin is roughly 38x, so the criteria very likely hold at the E005
  population — but widening the benchmark needs the two datasets to coexist,
  which T057 has just deliberately separated.

  pip-audit has produced no result on either side: it cannot run locally (TLS
  interception) and its CI step has not executed yet. Recorded as unmeasured
  rather than as a null result.

  The security limitation's reversal trigger has fired for /src/web — 3 high
  advisories on production dependencies. Upgrading `next` across a major is
  E001 scaffold work with its own verification surface.

  eslint reports 2 warnings, 0 errors, neither in E010's files: an unused
  `readFileSync` in `src/web/__tests__/boundary.test.ts` (E001's file, which
  E010 has never modified), and an unused directive inside the generated
  `src/web/coverage/` output. That directory is excluded by `.gitignore` and by
  `.prettierignore` but not by `eslint.config.mjs`'s `globalIgnores`, so it is
  linted whenever a coverage run precedes a lint run. Both live in E001's
  toolchain configuration.

  On a Windows checkout with `core.autocrlf=true`, `npx prettier --check .`
  reports 4 files in src/web as unformatted. They are not: the same content as
  stored in git passes `prettier --check --stdin-filepath`. The difference is
  CRLF in the working tree against the LF that is committed, so the CI gate on
  Linux is unaffected. Recorded so the next reader does not chase it.
